    "<p><strong>Percentage change:</strong> an increase of $p\\,\\%$ means multiplying by $1 + \\frac{p}{100}$, a decrease means multiplying by $1 - \\frac{p}{100}$.\n       A price of 80 € after a $25\\,\\%$ discount is $80\\cdot 0.75 = 60$ €.</p>",
